[{"id":77420,"sender_id":457,"sender_full_name":"jesuslop","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/110115442c5fa2fffecefb49120fb545?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/5-nLab-General-Discussions/topic/Stabilizer.20group/near/77420\">#1</a> Hi, at <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/stabilizer+group\">Stabilizer Group</a>, the notation for action groupoid used (one slash) seems not to fit with the one at <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/action+groupoid\">action groupoid</a> (two slashes). Not changing myself for the sake of prudence.</p>","timestamp":1560604772,"subject":"Stabilizer group","stream_id":5,"display_recipient":"nLab General Discussions","reactions":[]},{"id":77424,"sender_id":25,"sender_full_name":"David_Corfield","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/7d52fbe20c8ac05886a296e9ee2159b1?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/5-nLab-General-Discussions/topic/Stabilizer.20group/near/77424\">#2</a> Yes, that’s right. I’ve changed what I could see there to <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">/</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">/</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">//</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">//</span></span></span></span>. Sometimes people use \\sslash, but not all browsers show it. I see that another option is /!!/. Let’s compare:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">/</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">/</mi><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">X//G</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0785em;\">X</span><span class=\"mord\">//</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">G</span></span></span></span></li>\n<li><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">/</mi><mtext> ⁣</mtext><mtext> ⁣</mtext><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">/</mi><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">X/\\!\\!/G</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0785em;\">X</span><span class=\"mord\">/</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:-0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:-0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">/</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">G</span></span></span></span></li>\n<li><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace=\"0.22em\" rspace=\"0.22em\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">/</mi><mspace width=\"-0.3333em\"/><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">/</mi></mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">X\\mathbin{/\\mkern-6mu/} G</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0785em;\">X</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\"><span class=\"mord\">/</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:-0.3333em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">/</span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">G</span></span></span></span></li>\n</ul>","timestamp":1560673119,"subject":"Stabilizer group","stream_id":5,"display_recipient":"nLab General Discussions","reactions":[]},{"id":77425,"sender_id":457,"sender_full_name":"jesuslop","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/110115442c5fa2fffecefb49120fb545?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/5-nLab-General-Discussions/topic/Stabilizer.20group/near/77425\">#3</a> Thanks for updating, the three options render ok here in Chrome and Edge in Windows.</p>","timestamp":1560678301,"subject":"Stabilizer group","stream_id":5,"display_recipient":"nLab General Discussions","reactions":[]},{"id":77427,"sender_id":11,"sender_full_name":"Urs","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/b00d1ee17463af676c78974439b92471?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/5-nLab-General-Discussions/topic/Stabilizer.20group/near/77427\">#4</a> I find that <code>\\sslash</code> gets two much whitespace besides it (same problem in LaTeX, too). It looks better when done as</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\"><pre><code> X\\!\\!\\sslash\\!\\!G\n</code></pre>\n</div><p>to get <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mtext> ⁣</mtext><mtext> ⁣</mtext><mo lspace=\"0.22em\" rspace=\"0.22em\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">/</mi><mspace width=\"-0.3333em\"/><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">/</mi></mo><mtext> ⁣</mtext><mtext> ⁣</mtext><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">X\\!\\!\\mathbin{/\\mkern-6mu/}\\!\\!G</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0785em;\">X</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:-0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:-0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\"><span class=\"mord\">/</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:-0.3333em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">/</span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:-0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:-0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">G</span></span></span></span>.</p>\n<p>In my local LaTeX code I am happy to implement this way. Here on the nLab I am hesitant, because we never know if some time in the future the default typesetting of special characters such as <code>\\sslash</code> will change.</p>\n<p>In this respect, while not perfect, the hack <code>X/\\!\\!/G</code> might be better, since it is more unlikely that the spacing of the plain slash will ever be changed.</p>","timestamp":1560685629,"subject":"Stabilizer group","stream_id":5,"display_recipient":"nLab General Discussions","reactions":[]},{"id":77429,"sender_id":10,"sender_full_name":"Mike Shulman","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/ede34282f405f902e12fa7e6cf336572?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/5-nLab-General-Discussions/topic/Stabilizer.20group/near/77429\">#5</a> I expect that is because <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo lspace=\"0.22em\" rspace=\"0.22em\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">/</mi><mspace width=\"-0.3333em\"/><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">/</mi></mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathbin{/\\mkern-6mu/}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">/</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:-0.3333em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">/</span></span></span></span></span> is a <code>mathbin</code>; writing <code>X \\mathbin{/} G</code> in LaTeX gives it an equal amount of space.  I’m not sure what kind of symbol <code>/</code> is, but writing <code>X\\mathord{\\sslash} G</code> in LaTeX reduces its space to within spitting distance of <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">/</mi><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">X/G</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0785em;\">X</span><span class=\"mord\">/</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">G</span></span></span></span>.  That seems a somewhat more principled option than adding negative space around it (and probably likely to look better in some cases too; I’ve found that sometimes when LaTeX is squeezing things to fit on a line it makes my negative spaces become actually negative and thus overlaps some characters).  We can’t do that here, but maybe Richard could change something about the MathML generated by <code>\\sslash</code>?  I don’t know what the analogous options are for MathML.</p>","timestamp":1560696405,"subject":"Stabilizer group","stream_id":5,"display_recipient":"nLab General Discussions","reactions":[]},{"id":77437,"sender_id":237,"sender_full_name":"Richard Williamson","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/b90dbe6063b47a44f7308efebb6ade2b?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/5-nLab-General-Discussions/topic/Stabilizer.20group/near/77437\">#6</a> Hi, I’m happy to change it if I can (probably I can), but from a quick glance at the above discussion I’m not sure exactly what I should change it to. Could somebody summarise?</p>","timestamp":1560716676,"subject":"Stabilizer group","stream_id":5,"display_recipient":"nLab General Discussions","reactions":[]}]